## 2. Objective & Scope Description
Integrate the Control Tower operational framework directly into the application interface, establishing a unified dashboard that links project management views, evidence ledgers, real GitHub PR/task states, and read-only version health checks (V1–V4). All static mockup components must be purged and replaced with real structural data bindings adhering to our strict static GitHub Pages security model[span_6](start_span)[span_6](end_span).

## 3. Technical Requirements & Constraints
- **Zero Mock Data:** Complete and permanent removal of placeholder arrays, seed states, and "mock mode" banners.
- **Read-Only Security Model:** Adhere strictly to static hosting rules (no secrets, no server-side environment variables, safe GET routes only via `ui/js/config.js`)[span_7](start_span)[span_7](end_span).
- **Version Isolation:** Maintain strict boundaries between V1, V2, V3, and V4 modules with zero cross-contamination of state or unapproved backend calls[span_8](start_span)[span_8](end_span).
- **CSP & Allow-Lists:** Maintain explicit Content Security Policy headers restricting network connections to `api.github.com` and approved read-only worker endpoints[span_9](start_span)[span_9](end_span).

